Field_1 and Field_2 both require 4 drones for full protection, while Field_4 requires 3 and Field_3 only requires 2. As no drones are currently flying to any fields and all drones are idle, we should prioritize the fields with the highest threat levels and the most drones required for full protection.

Among the fields, Field_1 (threat level 0.15) and Field_2 (threat level 0.11) pose the highest threat levels. Next in line are Field_4 (threat level 0.11) and Field_3 (threat level 0.05). Since we have 8 idle drones available, we can send the following distribution:

- 4 drones to Field_1 (to fully protect it)
- 2 drones to Field_2 (to protect it partially, as we don't have enough drones for full protection)
- 2 drones can remain idle

This is a strategic allocation to reduce crop damage effectively, as Field_1 is the most threatened and should be prioritized for full protection.

